*.launch.log
dev.log
mobile.log

# Generated whole-repo source dumps.
#
# PROJECT_SOURCE.md was one of these, and it published the live service_role key
# — the credential that bypasses RLS on every table, including patient medical
# history — to this public repo on 2026-07-26. Anything that concatenates the
# whole tree will sweep up a .env value sooner or later, so these stay untracked.
PROJECT_SOURCE.md
*_SOURCE.md
project-source.*

# Leftover isolated agent worktrees (Agent tool, isolation: "worktree")
.claude/worktrees/

# Isolated Gradle home for local builds — must never be inside the archive
.gradle-isolated/
apks/

# Local build outputs — must never enter the eas project archive
*.tar.gz
queue-*.apk

# Pre-monorepo native husks, superseded by apps/client and apps/doctor. They hold
# no source — just android/ build output, node_modules and .expo — but each carries
# a real .env.local, and they were untracked *and* unignored, so a `git add -A` from
# the repo root would have staged those secrets. Same failure mode as PROJECT_SOURCE.md
# above. Kept on disk deliberately; ignored so they can never be committed.
/mobile/
/doctors/
